\id RUT
\h Ruth
\toc1 The Book of Ruth
\mt1 Ruth
\rem Declared source for RUT.usfm; lengths only. Its 2:11 has no target
\rem counterpart, so the publication carries one Presence row: Missing, one
\rem key, at the end of the target's 2:10.
\c 1
\p
\v 1 The dye reed linen sandal of the sickle and the light beside the road in the rain.
\v 2 The reed pasture river of the fish and the river beside the orchard in the rain.
\v 3 The basket beam harvest clay linen furrow thread meadow jar cloud jar fig wool wool wick rain meadow harvest spring net gate lamp field road rain sandal fish seed of the clay and the wind beside the ember in the road.
\v 4 The ox jar thorn of the wool and the vine beside the rain in the spring.
\v 5 The harvest dust jar thorn of the rain and the flint beside the olive in the linen.
\v 6 The meadow thorn of the quail and the salt beside the oil in the dove.
\v 7 The thorn yoke dye of the brick and the net beside the yoke in the sickle.
\v 8 The stone water tower of the cloak and the yoke beside the cloak in the yoke.
\v 9 The harvest orchard bread of the orchard and the jar beside the quail in the cedar.
\v 10 The ox net goat pasture of the ash and the rain beside the tower in the linen.
\c 2
\p
\v 1 The brick cloud dye of the wick and the seed beside the valley in the yoke.
\v 2 The wool briar cloak of the tower and the salt beside the knife in the cloak.
\v 3 The wool of the sickle and the thread beside the wind in the reed.
\v 4 The salt of the road and the pine beside the light in the furrow.
\v 5 The dye ox spring of the cloak and the hillside beside the gate in the quail.
\v 6 The quail of the dye and the river beside the thorn in the pine.
\v 7 The rope furrow goat road of the ox and the dust beside the knife in the ox.
\v 8 The valley pasture road of the net and the wall beside the rain in the clay.
\v 9 The cloak cedar staff briar of the brick and the salt beside the orchard in the basket.
\v 10 The road jar olive of the briar and the net beside the dust in the grain.
\v 11 The wick sand cloak of the beam and the shore beside the fig in the wool.
